# Every service's Dockerfile builds with `context: .` (repo root) but
# only ever COPYs specific services/ subdirectories -- without this
# file, `docker build`/`docker compose build` still tars up and uploads
# everything else under the repo root as build context first, including
# the real, potentially very large runtime data directories this same
# repo root also holds (library/, state/ -- state/device_backups/ alone
# was measured at 199GB live, see notes.md) and every credential file
# under config/secrets/. None of that should ever leave the filesystem
# as build context, whether for size or for secrecy.

library/
state/
config/secrets/
.env

.git/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
